hello my name is sarah dickerson  i'm a scientist at horizon discovery and  i will be presenting this poster on  crispr a using synthetic guide rna  so synthetic guide rna is beneficial in  many respects  for example it allows for short-term  expression and enables you to avoid  cloning which are some of the challenges  associated with using express guide rnas  crispr can be repurposed from a gene  editing tool to a transcriptional  regulation system  a nucleus deficient mutant of cas9 known  as dkas9  does not cleave the dna but retains the  ability to bind  guide rnas and localize to the target  dna  when dcas9 is fused to a transcriptional  regulator  it can activate transcription commonly  referred to as  crispr a several crispr a systems have  been developed  including suntag sam and vpr which we  show here  initially researchers used express  signal guide rnas for crisp array  and in data not shown we have found that  the synthetic two-part crispr rna and  tracer rna system  can also be used to activate  transcription with crispr a systems  here we investigate the use of a five  prime and modification of the crispr rna  and the three prime end modification of  the tracer rna in performing crispr  a we wanted to see if these  modifications would have an effect  on activation so we compared modified  crispr rna tracer rna  which is shown in dark green to  unmodified shown in light green  for four different genes and then  measure transcriptional activation  via r2 qpcr here we show  transcriptional fold activation for an  individual crispr rnas as well as the  pools of four  modifications allow for a dramatic  increase in activation  additionally the pull of four crispr  rnas also greatly enhance  activation for example there is a more  than  30-fold increase in activation of titan  with modified crispr rnas pooled  compared to unmodified crispr rnase  to determine how synthetic guide rna is  compared to  express single guide rna and lentiviral  expression  we compare the three methods for four  gene targets and report that synthetic  crispr rna trace rna result in gene  activation comparable to expressed  single guide rna  synthetic crispr rna and trace rna can  also be used with the sam system  sam is unique in that it uses a scaffold  tracer rna with an ms2 aptamer sequence  that recruits transcriptional activators  we found that the transcriptional  activation using either the sam or the  vpr system for six genes was comparable  there was no consistent trend across all  genes for example  transcriptional activation by sam was  higher for titan  whereas transcriptional activation for  vpr was higher for  l1 receptor 2. while most of the work  presented here  involves u2os cells stably expressing  dcas9 and their respective activators  we also demonstrate the effectiveness in  using synthetic  guide rnas with dcas9 vpr  mrna furthermore the advantage to using  either pure myosin dcas9vpr mrna or  egfp dcas9vpr mrna  is that it allows for enrichment  it is important to note that the basal  expression level of the target gene  may impact the level of activation  achievable  the bar graph represents transcriptional  activation ranked highest to lowest  for 23 different genes the endogenous  gene expression for each gene target  obtained from  rna-seq data is shown on the right  y-axis  we consistently found that genes that  have very low endogenous expression  levels  are typically activated to a higher  degree  for instance endogenous expression of l1  receptor 2  is very low so we are able to achieve a  dramatic increase  in activation with crispr a  synthetic guide rnas are also effective  for multiplexing  in which more than one gene may be  activated we demonstrate  that the level of transcriptional  activation achieved is similar  whether a single gene two genes or three  genes are simultaneously activated  synthetic crispr a crispr rna tracer rna  also enables pulled screening in an  arrayed format  as shown here using a cell line stably  expressing dcas9vpr  allows for fast and effective screening  u2sl stably expressing dcas9vpr  were transfected with the crispr a  library  consisting of 153 cytokine receptor  targets  where each well contained a pool of four  crisprna tracer rnas targeting one gene  also secretion was monitored by elisa  and then we were able to identify  al-6 regulators and here we identify  positive regulators of all six in red  and  negative regulators shown here in blue  so the work presented here shows that  synthetic guide rna can be successfully  used with crispr a systems like vpr  and sam multiple crispr rnas targeting  the same gene can be pulled to achieve  higher transcriptional activation of the  target gene  we also demonstrate that synthetic  crispr rna tracer rna  is ideal for simultaneous activation of  multiple genes  and is effective when used with  mrna and finally we showed that  synthetic guide rna can be used  for high throughput arrayed screening  applications  thank you for listening and please feel  free to reach out if you have any  questions  you
 

